<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pangeran Tumenggung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pangeran Tumenggung was a king of Negara Daha in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> who, according to the Banjar chronicle, seized the throne after the death of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja-sukarama">Maharaja Sukarama</a>. His nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-suriansyah">Raden Samudra</a>, the rightful heir, fled to the coast and with help from Demak defeated him, founding the Banjar Sultanate in 1526.</p></div>
